Inspect the bare repository in 'container/.bare'.
From '.bare', add a worktree at '../main' checking out branch 'main'.
Add a second worktree at '../feature' on a new branch 'feature'.
Verify that 'container/main/.git' is a pointer file rather than a directory.
Exit the subshell.

Tidbit: In a bare repository, 'git worktree add <path> <branch>' checks out
an existing branch, while '-b <new-branch>' creates one.
